quran[11]{c,v,t}:
  32,1,"Alif, Lam, Mim."
  32,2,"The revelation of the Book, there is no doubt in it, is from the Lord of all worlds."
  32,3,Do they say: ‘He has fabricated it?’ No! It is the truth from your Lord so that you may warn a people to whom no warner has come before you—that perhaps they may be guided (to the right path).
  32,4,"Allah is the One Who created the heavens and the earth and whatever is between them in six periods. Then He established (His authority) over the Throne (befitting His Glory). Apart from Him, you have neither any protector nor intercessor. Will you not then become mindful (of advice)?"
  32,5,He governs every affair from the heavens to the earth. Then it all ascends to Him in a day whose measure is a thousand years by your counting.
  32,6,"That is the Knower of the Unseen and the seen—the All-Mighty, the All-Merciful,"
  32,7,Who perfected everything that He created and originated the creation of humankind from clay.
  32,8,"Then, He made his progeny from an extract of an ignoble fluid."
  32,9,"Then, He proportioned him and breathed into him from His spirit. Then He made for you ears, eyes and hearts. Yet you hardly give thanks."
  32,10,"Still, they say (mockingly): ‘When we are lost in the earth, shall we certainly be (raised) in a new creation?’ Instead, they disbelieve in the meeting of their Lord."
  32,11,"Say: ‘The angel of death, who has been given charge of you, will take you (i.e. your soul) away. Then to your Lord, you shall be returned.’"
